      ":question/id": "92a9b2e3-9000-5a42-9686-423018101fb1",
      ":question/problem": "Without using a calculator, find the exact value of\n$$\n4\\,\\sin\\left(33.75^\\circ\\right)\\cos\\left(33.75^\\circ\\right)\\cos\\left(67.5^\\circ\\right).\n$$\nUse $2\\sin x\\cos x=\\sin(2x)$, first with $x=33.75^\\circ$ and then with $x=67.5^\\circ$.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Let $E$ denote the given expression. Use $\\sin x\\cos x=\\frac{1}{2}\\sin(2x)$ first at $x=33.75^\\circ$ and then at $x=67.5^\\circ$. Each application introduces a factor of $\\frac{1}{2}$.\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nE&=2\\,\\sin\\left(67.5^\\circ\\right)\\cos\\left(67.5^\\circ\\right)\\\\&=\\sin\\left(135^\\circ\\right)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\nThe terminal sine is $\\sin\\left(135^\\circ\\right)=\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}$.\nTherefore,\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nE&=\\left(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\right)\\\\&=\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$",
